@startuml

title 12.1. Admin reference and inventory UI completion

hide circle
skinparam linetype ortho

entity Currency
entity Unit
entity InventoryReason
entity InventoryDocument
entity InventoryDocumentLine
entity StockMovement
entity StatusHistory

class CurrencyController <<admin>>
class UnitController <<admin>>
class InventoryReasonController <<admin>>
class InventoryDocumentController <<admin>>
class StatusTimelineComponent <<twig>>

CurrencyController --> Currency : manage if editable
UnitController --> Unit : manage per store
InventoryReasonController --> InventoryReason : manage stock reasons
InventoryDocumentController --> InventoryDocument : inspect documents
InventoryDocument --> InventoryDocumentLine : lines
InventoryDocumentLine --> StockMovement : posted movements
InventoryDocumentController --> StatusTimelineComponent : show status history
StatusTimelineComponent --> StatusHistory : render generic timeline

note right of Currency
  Current status:
  - Currency entity and fixtures exist.
  - Store, documents, payments and prices use Currency.
  - No dedicated Currency admin controller exists.

  Decision:
  - If currencies stay dictionary-only, document that they are fixture/admin
    seed data and do not add UI.
  - If store admins must edit them, add a restricted admin CRUD
    with strong guards because historical documents depend on currencies.
end note

note right of Unit
  Current status:
  - Unit entity exists and Product forms use it.
  - No dedicated Unit admin CRUD exists.

  Required completion:
  - Add Unit index/new/edit/show scoped by Store.
  - Use inactive/deletedAt instead of destructive removal.
  - Keep old product/order snapshots readable.
end note

note right of InventoryReason
  Current status:
  - InventoryReason entity exists.
  - Inventory documents can reference a reason.
  - No full admin workflow exists for maintaining reason dictionary.

  Required completion:
  - Add InventoryReason CRUD/filter scoped by Store.
  - Validate store + type + name uniqueness.
  - Use inactive/deletedAt for archive behavior.
end note

note right of InventoryDocument
  Current status:
  - Backend posting/cancel/reversal exists.
  - StatusHistory is written for post/cancel.
  - There is no dedicated admin list/show for InventoryDocument.

  Required completion:
  - Add read-first admin index/show for InventoryDocument.
  - Show document header, lines, stock movements and linked business document.
  - Reuse generic status timeline component.
  - Keep post/cancel actions CSRF-protected and permission checked.
end note

note bottom
  Suggested implementation order:

  1. Add Unit admin CRUD because Product forms already depend on it.
  2. Add InventoryReason admin CRUD for stock adjustment/write-off flows.
  3. Add read-only InventoryDocument index/show with line/movement details.
  4. Attach StatusHistory timeline to InventoryDocument show.
  5. Decide whether Currency CRUD is needed or document fixture-only policy.
  6. Add controller tests for store scoping, soft archive and timeline render.
end note

@enduml
